# The journey north across seed 1: wake on the south coast, walk inland, then
# stand in each ecotone and walk across it, so the land can be seen turning.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/journey.tour --seed=1
# Every ecotone and the caldera are asked for by NAME. One coordinate is left,
# and the note on it says why.
zoom 30
shot 01-spawn
walk 0,-1 2.5 run
shot 02-inland
# coast into moss (asked for by name: the old 307,355 is coast heartland now)
place coast-moss
shot 03-coast-moss with border:coast-moss
walk 0,-1 2.5 run
shot 04-coast-moss-walked with land:coast|moss
# moss into pinewood
place moss-pinewood
shot 05-moss-pinewood with border:moss-pinewood
walk 1,-1 2.5 run
shot 06-moss-pinewood-walked with land:moss|pinewood
# over the water: the snow meeting the mesas on the next continent (GEN 24:
# the pinewood and the snow no longer share one)
place snowfield-mesas
shot 07-snowfield-mesas with border:snowfield-mesas
walk 0,-1 2.5 run
shot 08-snowfield-mesas-walked with land:snowfield|mesas
# snow to the rim of the burning
place snowfield-burning
shot 09-snowfield-burning with border:snowfield-burning
walk -1,-1 2.5 run
shot 10-snowfield-burning-walked with land:snowfield|burning
# A fumarole field out on the Burning's slopes. THE COORDINATE STAYS, and the
# claim is what guards it now. `place fumarole` was tried and looked at: it
# resolves to the first vent in the world's list, which on seed 1 stands on a
# spit with the sea taking half the frame — a worse picture of the same thing.
# This tile is an ash field with seven or eight vents burning in it, which is
# what "a fumarole field" means. So instead of moving the frame, the frame now
# has to PROVE it found vents: `prop:vent` is asked again at the shutter, and a
# worldgen change that takes the vents away fails the tour instead of filing a
# picture of empty ash under the name "fumarole".
# (GEN 24 moved the Burning to another continent, and the coordinate into the
# sea: the field is now found by name, the Burning's heart and its nearest vent.)
place burning
near vent
shot 11-fumarole with land:burning,prop:vent
# The caldera, which is a landmark and therefore has a name. This was
# `at 134,142`, the caldera's own tile on seed 1 to the half-tile.
place caldera
zoom 44
shot 12-caldera with land:burning
